          "text": "Initial gastrointestinal symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 6 days ago, after a night shift, developed nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. During the first 1–2 days: watery diarrhea up to approximately 8 times per day, 3–4 episodes of vomiting, and crampy lower abdominal pain. No blood or mucus in stool."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Gastrointestinal symptom progression"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Over the last 2–3 days, no vomiting, appetite has returned, and diarrhea has decreased to 2–3 loose stools per day. No nocturnal diarrhea. Mild bloating and cramps."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
